## PRODUCTION CRITICAL FILES — MINIMAL CHANGES ONLY
These files require explicit approval before modification.
Changes must be additive only: no reformatting, no restructuring, no refactoring existing code.

### Protected Files
- `backend/app/websocket/bridge_server.py` (production WebSocket backbone)
- `backend/app/main.py` (application lifespan + service initialization)
- `backend/app/services/littlenate_inference.py` (core inference pipeline)
- `backend/app/services/nate_memory_crystallizer.py` (crystal promotion engine)
- `docker-compose.prod.yml` (production deployment config)
- `backend/migrations/*.sql` (database schema — additive only, never ALTER/DROP existing)

### Rules for Protected Files
1. Maximum 50 lines changed per commit.
2. No reformatting or whitespace-only changes to existing code.
3. No moving or renaming existing functions.
4. New code must be behind a feature flag.
5. Every change must include a comment: `# QUANTUM-CRYSTAL-ARCH` or `# SOVEREIGN-VOICE`.
6. If Composer/agent proposes more than 50 lines changed, stop and ask for explicit approval.

